  {
   "id": "singing-a-tune",
   "title": {
    "en": "Singing a tune"
   },
   "colour": 4,
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "4-words",
     "title": {
      "en": "Following the words"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "In a song, each word sits on a note. Watch the words light up as you sing."
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Sing the first line of Amazing Grace with the guide."
       },
       "template": "amazing-grace",
       "singers": 4,
       "part": "soprano",
       "phrases": [
        0
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "4-phrasing",
     "title": {
      "en": "Phrasing"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "A phrase is one breath's worth of song. Breathe at the end of each line, not in the middle of a word."
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Sing two lines of Amazing Grace, breathing between them."
       },
       "template": "amazing-grace",
       "singers": 4,
       "part": "soprano",
       "phrases": [
        0,
        1
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "4-challenge",
     "title": {
      "en": "Amazing Grace, verse 1"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "record",
       "text": {
        "en": "The unit's challenge: record the melody of Amazing Grace, verse 1."
       },
       "template": "amazing-grace",
       "singers": 4,
       "part": "soprano"
      }
     ],
     "challenge": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "first-harmony",
   "title": {
    "en": "Your first harmony"
   },
   "colour": 5,
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "5-drone",
     "title": {
      "en": "Hum against a drone"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "Harmony is two notes at once. Hum the drone's note, then the note above it, then the one below, while the drone keeps going."
       },
       "listen": {
        "tempo": 72,
        "notes": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "length": 3,
          "step": 0,
          "lyric": "mm"
         }
        ],
        "turn": false,
        "drone": {
         "step": 0
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "play",
       "text": {
        "en": "Sing with the drone: the same note, then above, then below."
       },
       "exercise": {
        "tempo": 72,
        "notes": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "length": 3,
          "step": 0,
          "lyric": "mm"
         },
         {
          "beat": 3,
          "length": 3,
          "step": 4,
          "lyric": "mm"
         },
         {
          "beat": 6,
          "length": 3,
          "step": -3,
          "lyric": "mm"
         }
        ],
        "turn": false,
        "drone": {
         "step": 0
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "5-third",
     "title": {
      "en": "Find the third"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "A third is the sweetest harmony: two notes, one step apart on paper, that ring together. Listen to a note, then the third above it."
       },
       "listen": {
        "tempo": 72,
        "notes": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "length": 2,
          "step": 0,
          "lyric": "oo"
         },
         {
          "beat": 2,
          "length": 2,
          "step": 4,
          "lyric": "oo"
         }
        ],
        "turn": false
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "play",
       "text": {
        "en": "A note plays: sing the third above it while it keeps sounding."
       },
       "exercise": {
        "tempo": 72,
        "notes": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "length": 4,
          "step": 4,
          "lyric": "oo"
         }
        ],
        "turn": false,
        "drone": {
         "step": 0
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "play",
       "text": {
        "en": "Now the third below."
       },
       "exercise": {
        "tempo": 72,
        "notes": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "length": 4,
          "step": -3,
          "lyric": "oo"
         }
        ],
        "turn": false,
        "drone": {
         "step": 0
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "5-round",
     "title": {
      "en": "A round"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "In a round, everyone sings the same tune, starting at different times. The harmony happens by itself."
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Learn the 2nd voice of Are You Sleeping, which starts two bars after the 1st."
       },
       "template": "are-you-sleeping",
       "singers": 2,
       "part": "alto"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "5-thirds",
     "title": {
      "en": "Two parts in thirds"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Learn the alto of Michael, Row the Boat Ashore, a third below the tune."
       },
       "template": "michael-row",
       "singers": 2,
       "part": "alto"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "5-challenge",
     "title": {
      "en": "Record the round's 2nd voice"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "record",
       "text": {
        "en": "The unit's challenge: record the 2nd voice of Are You Sleeping."
       },
       "template": "are-you-sleeping",
       "singers": 2,
       "part": "alto"
      }
     ],
     "challenge": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "low-and-inner",
   "title": {
    "en": "Low and inner voices"
   },
   "colour": 6,
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "6-bass",
     "title": {
      "en": "The bass line"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "The bass sings the chord's roots, the floor the others stand on. It moves less, and sings \"oo\"."
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Learn the bass of Amazing Grace, for 3 singers."
       },
       "template": "amazing-grace",
       "singers": 3,
       "part": "bass"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "6-tenor",
     "title": {
      "en": "The tenor"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Learn the tenor of Amazing Grace, the inner voice that fills the chord."
       },
       "template": "amazing-grace",
       "singers": 4,
       "part": "tenor"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "6-hold",
     "title": {
      "en": "Hold your note"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "Holding your note while the harmony moves around you is the heart of singing a part. The chords change; your note stays."
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "play",
       "text": {
        "en": "Hold your note as the chords move."
       },
       "exercise": {
        "tempo": 66,
        "notes": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "length": 8,
          "step": 0,
          "lyric": "oo"
         }
        ],
        "turn": false,
        "chords": [
         {
          "beat": 0,
          "root": 0,
          "quality": "maj",
          "bass": null
         },
         {
          "beat": 2,
          "root": 5,
          "quality": "maj",
          "bass": 0
         },
         {
          "beat": 4,
          "root": 9,
          "quality": "min",
          "bass": null
         },
         {
          "beat": 6,
          "root": 0,
          "quality": "maj",
          "bass": null
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "6-challenge",
     "title": {
      "en": "Record the bass of Amazing Grace"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "record",
       "text": {
        "en": "The unit's challenge: record the bass of Amazing Grace."
       },
       "template": "amazing-grace",
       "singers": 3,
       "part": "bass"
      }
     ],
     "challenge": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "whole-song",
   "title": {
    "en": "The whole song is you"
   },
   "colour": 7,
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "7-blend",
     "title": {
      "en": "Hearing the blend"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "kind": "learn",
       "text": {
        "en": "When every part is your voice, listen to how they sit together. A part that's too loud or late stands out; nudge and balance it in the studio."
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "use",
       "text": {
        "en": "Sing the alto of Amazing Grace with the other parts."
